The stat stuff ... Mec the Valkyrie, Level 16, 213 hit points, never
more than level 16 for the entire game.  AC -36, though.

I used 5 wishes: GoP, GDSM, Helm of Brilliance, magic marker, scroll of
charging.  I had two wishes left over when I ascended.  I had an AoLS
but it was never used.

No abuses: no polypiling, no wishing for quest artifacts or weapon artifacts,
no save file abuse, no paralysis abuse, no reading source code or r.g.h
while playing.

I had lots and lots of armor (most naturally occuring except for GDSM):
boots of speed (2), boots of water walking (2), boots of levitation,
boots of jumping.  The boots of jumping came in handy throughout the
game, especially on the Astral Plane.  A helm of opposite alignment helped
me climb through Gehennom much faster on the way back.  That plus some
useful scrolls which got me through the elemental planes fast meant I had
to kill the wiz only 4 times.

Stupid mistake #1 ... zapping an unknown wand at myself when it
wasn't having an effect on monsters (thought it might be slow or haste
and I could identify it).  It was cancellation.  Oops!  All my armor went
to +0 and all my wands become useless.

Stupid mistake #2 ... walking one space too far on the quest level right
into some lava.  Fzzt!  There go the water walking boots.

My strategy was: don't use anything before identifying it.  So I saved up
lots of potions and scrolls until I had several potions of water and
scrolls of identify, then ID'd everything.

Ob-feedback-to-dev-team: please take out most of those damn maze
levels, the game would be about the same with just a few of them.
Also, the weapon balance is just plain shot, I always get an artifact
weapon around level 3 or so.  Why not make these weapons the targets
of another miniquest?  Then people would have to use long swords and
two-handed swords and crys-knives longer.  On the plus side, I really
like the elemental levels.

Whew.  Ok, my nethack addiction is now over, at least until 3.2 comes out!

